    "field": "Ocean wave climate",
    "problem": "The paper addresses the challenge that estimating extreme wave conditions for engineering design assumes a stationary climate, but instrumental records show a significant increase in wave heights over 25 years, making it difficult to distinguish long-term trends from natural year-to-year variability.",
    "method": "To address long-term wave climate variability, the authors propose continuing measurements at specific sites for the immediate future, while ultimately using extensive satellite data on wave height and wind velocity combined with improved wave hindcast models to provide better spatial coverage and understanding.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze 25 years of instrumental wave data from the north-east Atlantic to determine if there has been a statistically significant long-term increase in wave height, a trend with major implications for designing offshore structures and coastal defenses.",
